<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Telugu Cholas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">11th–14th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Telugu Chodas, Nellore Cholas</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Telugu <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Cholas</a>, or Telugu Chodas, were families of chiefs in the Telugu country who claimed descent from the Tamil Chola kings. The most important line ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nellore">Nellore</a> in the 12th and 13th centuries, acting at times as feudatories of the Cholas and Kakatiyas; its ruler Manumasiddhi was patron of the poet Tikkana.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/telugu-cholas.jpg" alt="Telugu Cholas" width="320" height="166" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG Coins · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Telugu_Chodas_of_Nellore._Bhoja_II._1216-1316_CE._Uniface_flan_with_central_lion_standing_left,_four_additional_lion,_two_%C5%9Bri,_uncertain,_and_bhujabha_in_Kananda_punchmarks.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
